<speak>An airstrike killed at least one hundred fifty people at a school in Iran — scores of them children — near two Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps facilities, with analysts saying artificial intelligence targeting systems guided the strike. Neither the United States nor Israel has claimed the attack, though Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth confirmed the Pentagon is investigating and that children were among the dead. Investigators have not identified the munition or those who authorized it.

That's your briefing from zuhd news.

We return this evening in Makkah.

إن شاء الله.</speak>